{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795379210,"nonce":"HormM0Hm1P9CrgD0VtbYXs6gdxc=","title":"Move ash to beadie 0.4.0 and cranelift 0.138","message":"beadie 0.4.0 is on crates.io. beadie-cranelift in it uses crates.io cranelift 0.138 instead of the wasmtime git revision bc2f967 (0.136.0-dev), so ash's own cranelift-codegen, cranelift-frontend and cranelift-module move to 0.138 with it: a second release alongside beadie's would compile as an incompatible crate. The workspace now takes beadie from the registry, and no wasmtime git revision remains in Cargo.lock. wasmtime 43 still brings cranelift 0.130.2 separately, as before.\n\nNo source changes were needed in ash or ash_interp.\n\nChecks on macOS arm64: CI lint matrix (workspace, all features, no default features) clean; ash_core --lib 231 passed; cross_targets passed; the whole ash package, 63 test binaries, passed except unresolved_helper, which failed once on a timing race that is in the test and not in the dependency (filed as a301fdf, fixed in 40d5ae23).\n\nNUC (Linux x86_64, pinned to cores 0,2,4,6, interleaved with the base binary built from b2f6730c on the previous beadie): 13 benchmarks, hybrid-auto, 15 timed runs each. Nine rows within 2% on the median; nbody 480.5 vs 488.9 ms. The four rows the harness would not compare, fib, stdlib, jsonparse and nbody, were noisy: fib read +8.5% on the median with the fastest run +1.5% and the run times bimodal. Re-run with 40 timed runs on fib, stdlib, jsonparse, mandelbrot_small and deltablue: every row within 2.2% on both the median and the 25th percentile (fib +1.0%, stdlib -0.7%, jsonparse +1.1%, mandelbrot_small +2.2%, deltablue +1.3%).\n\nA first NUC attempt compared a stale binary with itself because the build was killed for memory; those numbers were discarded.","files":null}]}